Consent Management
===================
Checking the Consent Documents
-------------------------------

1. Log in to Castellum by using your username and password

   - Make sure you are connected to the WiFi and use your right username and
     password
     
2. Click on **Consent documents** and then on **Admin** on the front page

3. Scroll all the way down and press **Consent documents**
   
   - You will see a list of all consent documents that have been created
   - Additional information that will be shown to you: date of creation and
     whether the consent document is valid or not
     
Updating the Consent Documents
-------------------------------

It is possible for a consent document to become invalid because of 
- a change in the legislation
- a present date on which the validity expires
- ...

A) There are two options you may implement when a consent document becomes invalid
   - The consent form can be marked as **Is deprecated** or
   - If you uncheck the box saying **Is valid**, the consent document is marked
     as invalid


B) If you wish to upload a consent document that is currently valid, proceed as
   follows:
   
   - Click on **ADD CONSENT DOCUMENT** on the upper right
